<!--
  The `main` source set's copy of this file — what a RELEASE build
  actually gets (see `src/debug/res/xml/network_security_config.xml`'s
  doc comment for the full explanation and the crash this split fixed).
  Deliberately minimal: no domain-config, no cleartext exception — a
  release build must use HTTPS for every host, which is Android's own
  default behavior on API 28+ with no config file at all. This file
  exists only so `android:networkSecurityConfig="@xml/
  network_security_config"` in AndroidManifest.xml always resolves to
  SOMETHING for every build variant; it intentionally grants nothing
  beyond the platform default.
-->
